{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 20,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wine ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a mocker, strong drink ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " raging: and whoever is deceived by it is not wise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The fear of a king ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as the roaring of a lion: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whoever",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " provoketh him to anger sinneth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "against",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his own soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an honor for a man to cease from strife: but every fool will be meddling.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The sluggard will not plow by reason of the cold; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "therefore",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall he beg in harvest, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "have",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Counsel in the heart of man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is like",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " deep water; but a man of understanding will draw it out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Most men will proclaim every one his own goodness: but a faithful man who can find?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The just ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " walketh in his integrity: his children ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " blessed after him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A king that sitteth on the throne of judgment scattereth away all evil with his eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who can say, I have made my heart clean, I am pure from my sin?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Divers weights, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " divers measures, both of them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " alike abomination to the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even a child is known by his doings, whether his work ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pure, and whether ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " right.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The hearing ear, and the seeing eye, the LORD hath made even both of them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Love not sleep, lest thou come to poverty; open thy eyes, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou shalt be satisfied with bread.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " naught, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " naught, saith the buyer: but when he is gone, then he boasteth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is gold, and a multitude of rubies: but the lips of knowledge ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a precious jewel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take his garment that is surety ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a stranger: and take a pledge of him for a strange woman.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Bread of deceit ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sweet to a man; but afterwards his mouth shall be filled with gravel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " purpose is established by counsel: and with good advice make war.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that goeth about ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a tale-bearer revealeth secrets; therefore meddle not with him that flattereth with his lips.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoever curseth his father or his mother, his lamp shall be put out in obscure darkness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "An inheritance ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "may be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " gotten hastily at the beginning; but the end of it shall not be blessed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Say not thou, I will recompense evil; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wait on the LORD, and he shall save thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Divers weights ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an abomination to the LORD; and a false balance ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Man's goings ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the LORD; how can a man then understand his own way?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a snare to the man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " devoureth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " holy, and after vows to make inquiry.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wise king scatterreth the wicked, and bringeth the wheel over them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The spirit of man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the candle of the LORD, searching all the inward parts of the belly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Mercy and truth preserve the king: and his throne is upheld by mercy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The glory of young men ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their strength: and the beauty of old men ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the gray head.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.20.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.20.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The blueness of a wound cleanseth away evil: so ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "do",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " stripes the inward parts of the belly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
